      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Ujjain</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle arrives at its destination, the delivery handover is a structured process designed to confirm the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and ownership documents. The procedure begins with a daylight re‑inspection that compares the current state of the bike to the photographs taken at pickup.</p>
<p>This visual check looks for scratches, dents, or any new damage that could indicate mishandling or theft during transit. Any discrepancies are noted and photographed for the client’s records.</p>

<p>Next, the odometer reading is verified against the mileage listed on the LR bilty. The delivery agent reads the instrument cluster, records the figure, and cross‑checks it with the bilty’s mileage entry.</p>
<p>A mismatch triggers a brief investigation to determine whether the discrepancy is due to a faulty gauge or a data entry error. The agent documents the reading and signs it in the delivery log to create a clear audit trail.</p>

<p>Following the mileage confirmation, the handover moves to the signed condition sign‑off stage. The client reviews the inspection report, confirms that all items match the pre‑delivery condition, and signs the delivery form.</p>
<p>The delivery agent also signs the same document, acknowledging that the vehicle has been inspected, the odometer verified, and the client’s approval received. This dual signature ensures mutual accountability and protects both parties from future disputes.</p>

<p>Finally, both parties retain copies of the signed handover sheet, the updated odometer record, and any photographic evidence. These documents are uploaded to the company’s digital platform for audit purposes and are also provided to the client in hard copy.</p>
<p>The completion of this process marks the official transfer of the motorcycle from the logistics team to the owner, closing the delivery cycle with transparency and trust.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



